## 3. Design direction (binding)

### Anti-pattern reference
The user's other project at
`C:\Users\gperuzzf\OneDrive - NTT DATA EMEAL\Documentos\ABI\Sandbox VSCode\stuff\martech_framework_pdf`
is heavily Apple-like / glassmorphic: translucent surfaces with
`backdrop-filter: blur(22px) saturate(155%)`, radii up to 28px, drop shadows like
`0 24px 70px rgba(15,23,42,0.18)`, multi-radial ambient gradients, animated orb
loaders, hero headings `clamp(2.4rem, 5.4vw, 4.8rem)`, gradient pill buttons
with hover lift. **This project must NOT adopt that look.**

### Do NOT introduce
- Glassmorphism or `backdrop-filter`.
- Multi-radial ambient gradients on layout chrome.
- Large drop shadows (`shadow-lg` and above) or colored shadows.
- Oversized rounded corners (anything above 16px).
- Animated decorative loaders, orb spinners, gradient buttons.
- Hero typography or marketing-style hero sections.
- Transform-based hover lifts.
- Multi-color brand gradients.

### Do adopt — flat minimalism (Linear / Notion / Stripe dashboards)
- Information density over whitespace. Power users want data, not breathing room.
- One primary task per screen; progressive disclosure for secondary info.
- 5–7 primary KPIs maximum (3–5 for executive views).
- Sidebar: 240–280px expanded, 64–72px collapsed.
- Main area uses CSS Grid with `auto-fill, minmax(...)`.
- Skeleton loaders, not spinners. Page interactive in under 2.5s.
- Sticky filters across navigation within a session.
- WCAG 2.2 AA baseline. Never rely on color alone — pair label, icon and color.
- Direct labels beat legends. Bar charts always start at zero. No 3D, no
  decorative fills.

