## 5. Chart presets — Tufte / Darkhorse "Data Looks Better Naked"

Reference: <https://darkhorsevisualization.com/blog/data-looks-better-naked>

Centralize these presets in `src/lib/chart-presets.ts` (or a sibling module) the
first time a chart-touching PR lands. Until then, every new Recharts usage MUST
mirror the exact props below.

```tsx
<CartesianGrid vertical={false} stroke="rgb(226 232 240)" strokeDasharray="3 3" />

<XAxis
  dataKey="..."
  axisLine={false}
  tickLine={false}
  tick={{ fontSize: 12, fill: "rgb(100 116 139)" }}
/>
<YAxis
  axisLine={false}
  tickLine={false}
  tick={{ fontSize: 12, fill: "rgb(100 116 139)" }}
  width={40}
/>

<Bar dataKey="..." fill="rgb(15 23 42)" radius={[2, 2, 0, 0]} />

<Line
  type="monotone"
  dataKey="..."
  stroke="rgb(15 23 42)"
  strokeWidth={2}
  dot={false}
  activeDot={{ r: 3 }}
/>

// Pie / Donut: avoid unless strictly required.
// When unavoidable: direct labels and at most 4 slices.
```

Additional chart rules:
- Always wrap in `<ResponsiveContainer>`. Container `min-h-[200px]`.
- Prefer direct labels on series. Only use `<Legend />` when there are 3+ series
  AND direct labeling is impractical; then `iconType="circle"`, `iconSize={8}`.
- Bar charts always start at zero. Never use truncated y-axes for emphasis.
- No 3D, no shadows, no decorative gradient fills. No background panels behind
  the chart — let it breathe inside its card.
- Tooltip: minimal custom component, `bg-white`, `border-slate-200`, no shadow
  stacking.
- Number formatting: `Intl.NumberFormat('pt-BR')` for counts. ISO or short month
  format for dates.

